fastp v1.3.6 paired-end QC and overlap adapter trimming
Inputs:
  forward.fastqsanger.gz (377,961 pairs)
  reverse.fastqsanger.gz (377,961 pairs)
Command:
  fastp -i forward.fastqsanger.gz -I reverse.fastqsanger.gz \
    -o trimmed_forward.fastqsanger.gz -O trimmed_reverse.fastqsanger.gz \
    -q 20 -u 40 -n 5 -l 15 -G --thread 4
Settings:
  low-quality base threshold: Phred < 20
  discard pair if either mate has >40% low-quality bases
  discard pair if either mate has >5 N bases
  discard pair if either mate is <15 bases after adapter trimming
  adapter trimming: paired-end overlap analysis only
  no adapter sequence supplied; no separate adapter-sequence autodetection
  no quality trimming, polyG trimming, or base correction enabled
Results:
  retained pairs: 277,113
  filtered reads failed low quality: 201,676
  filtered reads failed N limit: 20
  reads with adapter trimmed: 89,226
  adapter-trimmed bases: 2,091,846
  output mates synchronized: yes
Deliverables:
  final_answer/trimmed_forward.fastqsanger.gz
  final_answer/trimmed_reverse.fastqsanger.gz
